* PIC16(L)F1508/1509 Pin Definitions -- 20-Pin PDIP/SOIC/SSOP and
* 20-Pin QFN/UQFN (combined)
* Source: Microchip DS40001609F "PIC16(L)F1508/9 Microcontroller Data
*         Sheet" (also covers PIC12F1501/PIC16F1503/1507 as siblings
*         in the same family document set, but those are separate,
*         non-pin-compatible devices documented elsewhere), Pin
*         Diagrams section and Table 1-2 (Pinout Description).
*
* Primary device: PIC16F1509 -- determines this file's name.
*
* Companion devices -- PIC16F1508 and PIC16F1509 are peripheral-
* identical per Table 1-1 (Device Peripheral Summary): same 18 I/O,
* same 12-channel ADC, same comparators/timers/PWM/MSSP/EUSART/DAC/
* CLC/NCO/CWG counts -- differing ONLY in Flash (4096 vs 8192 words)
* and SRAM (256 vs 512 bytes), the standard memory-size-variant case
* used throughout this project. Includes the low-voltage "L" variants
* on the same basis as every other L-suffix device here (voltage/
* speed grade only). Per datasheet listing order:
*   PIC16F1508, PIC16LF1508, PIC16F1509, PIC16LF1509
*
* NOT included -- PIC12F1501 (8-pin), PIC16F1503 (14-pin), and
* PIC16F1507 (20-pin but only 12 I/O per Table 1-1, a genuinely
* smaller peripheral set) are covered by the same family overview
* page as this datasheet but are documented in SEPARATE datasheets
* (DS40001615, DS40001607, DS40001586 respectively) and are not
* pin-compatible with the 1508/1509 pair. Each would need its own
* file sourced from its own datasheet.
*
* Package scope -- 20-Pin PDIP/SOIC/SSOP and 20-Pin QFN/UQFN are
* combined into this single file. Both packages expose the exact
* same 20 physical pins (18 GPIO + MCLR-shared-RA3 counted within
* that 18 + VDD + VSS) with identical functions -- confirmed via the
* Pin Diagrams, which show both packages sharing one pin-allocation
* table (Table 1) with just two different physical numbering
* columns. No NC pins on either package -- unlike every prior multi-
* package family in this project, both variants here use exactly 20
* physical pins with no padding needed. The QFN/UQFN package also has
* an exposed bottom pad the datasheet recommends tying to VSS -- not
* a distinct signal, already covered by the G record.
*
* Flagged for manual review (dual-function / non-obvious pins):
*   RA3     -- CLC1IN0/VPP/T1G/SS/MCLR. UNLIKE every other GPIO pin
*             on this device (each explicitly documented as "General
*             purpose I/O") and unlike the MCLR pin on the PIC16F1847/
*             PIC16F1827 devices elsewhere in this project, Table 1-2
*             explicitly documents this pin's GPIO function as
*             "General purpose INPUT with IOC and WPU" -- Output Type
*             column reads "--" (no output driver at all). Classified
*             I (not B): this pin genuinely cannot drive an output
*             even when MCLR is disabled via config bits, confirmed
*             directly rather than assumed from precedent. This also
*             matches Table 1-1's Note 2 ("One pin is input-only").
*   RA4/RA5 -- CLKOUT/OSC2 and CLKIN/OSC1, oscillator-mode-dependent
*             alternate functions on otherwise ordinary GPIO pins
*             (both explicitly documented as "General purpose I/O").
*             Classified B, same reasoning as PIC16F1847/1827's
*             RA6/RA7 -- external oscillator mode is a config-bit
*             choice, not a pin dedication, on this enhanced mid-
*             range core.
*   Several pins (RA3, RC5, RC6) have alternate functions selectable
*   only via the APFCON (Alternate Pin Function) register rather than
*   being always active -- noted in the datasheet with superscript
*   (1) but not separately encoded here, same treatment as the PPS-
*   remappable RPn functions on the dsPIC33CK256MP505 elsewhere in
*   this project.

D PIC16(L)F1508/9 20-Pin PDIP/SOIC/SSOP/QFN/UQFN 8-bit Flash Microcontroller
P PIC16F1508 PIC16LF1508 PIC16F1509 PIC16LF1509

V VDD
B RA0 AN0/C1IN+/DAC1OUT1/ICSPDAT/ICDDAT
B RA1 AN1/CLC4IN1/VREF+/C1IN0-/C2IN0-/ICSPCLK/ICDCLK
B RA2 AN2/C1OUT/DAC1OUT2/T0CKI/INT/PWM3/CLC1/CWG1FLT
I RA3 CLC1IN0/VPP/T1G/SS/MCLR
B RA4 AN3/SOSCO/CLKOUT/T1G
B RA5 CLKIN/T1CKI/NCO1CLK/SOSCI
B RB4 AN10/CLC3IN0/SDA/SDI
B RB5 AN11/CLC4IN0/RX/DT
X 1
K SIMCLK

B RB6 SCL/SCK
B RB7 CLC3/TX/CK
B RC0 AN4/CLC2/C2IN+
B RC1 AN5/C1IN1-/C2IN1-/PWM4/NCO1
B RC2 AN6/C1IN2-/C2IN2-
B RC3 AN7/C1IN3-/C2IN3-/PWM2/CLC2IN0
B RC4 C2OUT/CLC2IN1/CLC4/CWG1B
B RC5 PWM1/CLC1/CWG1A
B RC6 AN8/NCO1/CLC3IN1/SS
B RC7 AN9/CLC1IN1/SDO
G VSS
